    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d402">

                <pb facs="0953" n="919" xml:id="pg919"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Conference files, lot 60 D 627, CF 212</note>
                <head>No. 402<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The President to the Secretary of
                        State</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d402-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">routine</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-02-01">February 1, 1954</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Many thanks for your informative reports. I find them valuable and extremely
                    interesting and hope you will continue to keep me up to date. I know that your
                    mission is a fatiguing one, but I know also that you are equal to every
                    requirement of your exacting task.</p>
                <p>With warm regard,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dwight D.
                    Eisenhower</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d402-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d402-f1-content">
                <p>Transmitted to Berlin in Tedul 14, Feb. 1. On Feb. 2 Secretary Dulles replied as
                    follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Many thanks your message which gives us encouragement. It is work
                            running late into every night. But we feel some real gains are being
                            made and whole delegation cooperating in fine spirit.” (Dulte 29 from
                            Berlin, Feb. 2, Conference files, lot 60 D 627, CF 212)</p>
                    </quote></p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
